    "https://www.alverno.edu/Career-Recent-Internships": {
      "title": "Career",
      "description": "Recent Internships | Career Studio | Alverno College https://alverno.studentadvisor.ai/virtualadvisor Alverno News Faculty Experts News/Blog Alverno Magazine Athletics Visit Events Alumnae Give My Alverno Search by Keywords\n                  Here Academics & Admissions Academics Majors and Programs List Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Adult Learning & Degree Completion Transfer Students International Students Tuition & Aid Tuition Financial Aid Scholarships Admissions Visit Meet an Admissions Counselor Accepted Students Support & Career Center for Academic Excellence Internships Only at Alverno Research Center for Women and Girls Thea Bowman Institute for Excellence and Leadership Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Catalogs & Policies Campus Visit Us The best way to know if Alverno is right for you is to come visit! About Alverno About A Hispanic-Serving Institution First-Generation College Students Where All Belong Alverno's President Campus Events Campus Life Residence Life Dining Services Student Engagement Greenhouse Campus Ministry Campus Safety Store A-Store (Alverno Gear) Resources Academic Academic Advising Career Studio Center for Learning and Assessment Support Library/Archives Student Development and Success Study Abroad Technology Media Hub Tech Services Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Accounts Student Accounts Financial Aid Health & Safety Wellness Campus Safety Additional Resources Resources for Parents All Student Resources Internal Event Brand Guide Alverno Publications Abilities 8 Abilities Center for Learning and Assessment Support Volunteer Assessor Program Assessment Workshops and Consulting Request Info Apply Menu Close Search by Keywords\n                  Here Academics & Admission Academics Majors and Programs List Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Adult Learning & Degree Completion Transfer Students International Students Tuition & Aid Tuition Financial Aid Scholarships Admissions Visit Meet an Admissions Counselor Accepted Students Support & Career Center for Academic Excellence Internships Only at Alverno Research Center for Women and Girls Thea Bowman Institute for Excellence and Leadership Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Catalogs & Policies Campus Visit Us About Alverno About A Hispanic-Serving Institution First-Generation College Students Where All Belong Alverno's President Campus Events Campus Life Residence Life Dining Services Student Activities Greenhouse Campus Ministry Campus Safety Store A-Store (Alverno Gear) Resources Academic Academic Advising Career Studio Instructional Services Library Student Development and Success Study Abroad Technology Media Hub Tech Services Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Accounts Student Accounts Financial Aid Health & Safety Wellness Campus Safety Additional Resources Resources for Parents All Student Resources Internal Event Brand Guide Alverno Publications 8 Abilities 8 Abilities Center for Learning and Assessment Support Volunteer Assessor Program Assessment Workshops & Consulting Alverno News Faculty Experts News/Blog A Magazine Apply Request Info Athletics Visit Events Alumnae Give My Alverno Career Student Resources Career Coaching Internship Advising Internship Advising Forms Recent Internships Handshake Alum Resources Handshake Employer Resources Hire an Intern Recruit a Grad Handshake Internship Forms Community Resources Online Resources Career Studio Team Office Hours & Contact Info Recent Internships Internships That Build Real-World Confidence Alverno students turn classroom learning into practical experience through internships and clinical placements that support every major. With a 100 percent internship and clinical\n        placement rate , our students gain hands-on experience, build confidence in professional settings and form connections that help launch their careers. Where Alverno Students Intern Placements include a mix of well-known organizations and mission-driven community partners. Students recently interned with organizations such as: Advocate Aurora Ascension Association of Equipment Manufacturers Autism Intervention LLC Bader Philanthropies ForwardDental Healthy Families Milwaukee County Medical College of Wisconsin Milwaukee Bucks Northwestern Mutual Pathfinders RoxArtMKE Soberalski Immigration Law The Parenting Network TurnUp Activism US Cellular United Community Center Walker’s Point Community Clinic These partnerships give students direct exposure to professional expectations, community impact and emerging career paths. Explore Opportunities Across Many Industries Students find internships in roles linked to their goals, strengths and interests. Recent internships fall into the following areas: Healthcare and Mental Health: Clinical support, patient services, behavioral therapy and health outreach roles with major systems and community clinics. Education and Youth Services: Academic departments, schools, community learning centers and youth-focused organizations. Business, Finance and Marketing: Corporate communications, business operations, finance and marketing roles in large companies and growing organizations. Nonprofit, Community and Social Impact: Philanthropy, community services, advocacy and human services positions supporting mission-driven work. Arts, Media and Creative Work: Studio, design and media assistant roles in creative environments. Civic Engagement and Public Service: Politics, public affairs and community engagement work with advocacy groups and local offices. Recent Internship Experiences Major Employer Role Psychology Medical College of Wisconsin Mental Health Services Intern Business and Management Milwaukee Bucks Marketing Intern Social Work Pathfinders Social Work Intern Biomedical Sciences Advocate Aurora Patient Care Associate Communication US Cellular Communications Intern Art RoxArtMKE Studio Assistant Ready to Discover Your Path? Alverno’s Career Studio helps students find internships that match their aspirations. Support includes resume review, interview preparation and personal guidance at each step. Your internship can be a meaningful step toward the life you want to build. Ready for what's next Request More Info Apply Now Explore Programs 3400 S. 43rd St. Milwaukee, WI 53219 414-382-6000 admissions@alverno.edu Campus Map Mesa Location Contact Us Employment at Alverno Event Spaces Faculty Directory Trustees Privacy Policy Faculty & Staff Intranet Accreditation Harassment/Discrimination Policy Web Accessibility Statement Institutional Review Board © Alverno College, All Rights Reserved"
    },
