      "title": "Employer Resources",
      "description": "Employer Resources | Career Studio | Alverno College https://alverno.studentadvisor.ai/virtualadvisor Alverno News Faculty Experts News/Blog Alverno Magazine Athletics Visit Events Alumnae Give My Alverno Search by Keywords\n                  Here Academics & Admissions Academics Majors and Programs List Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Adult Learning & Degree Completion Transfer Students International Students Tuition & Aid Tuition Financial Aid Scholarships Admissions Visit Meet an Admissions Counselor Accepted Students Support & Career Center for Academic Excellence Internships Only at Alverno Research Center for Women and Girls Thea Bowman Institute for Excellence and Leadership Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Catalogs & Policies Campus Visit Us The best way to know if Alverno is right for you is to come visit! About Alverno About A Hispanic-Serving Institution First-Generation College Students Where All Belong Alverno's President Campus Events Campus Life Residence Life Dining Services Student Engagement Greenhouse Campus Ministry Campus Safety Store A-Store (Alverno Gear) Resources Academic Academic Advising Career Studio Center for Learning and Assessment Support Library/Archives Student Development and Success Study Abroad Technology Media Hub Tech Services Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Accounts Student Accounts Financial Aid Health & Safety Wellness Campus Safety Additional Resources Resources for Parents All Student Resources Internal Event Brand Guide Alverno Publications Abilities 8 Abilities Center for Learning and Assessment Support Volunteer Assessor Program Assessment Workshops and Consulting Request Info Apply Menu Close Search by Keywords\n                  Here Academics & Admission Academics Majors and Programs List Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Adult Learning & Degree Completion Transfer Students International Students Tuition & Aid Tuition Financial Aid Scholarships Admissions Visit Meet an Admissions Counselor Accepted Students Support & Career Center for Academic Excellence Internships Only at Alverno Research Center for Women and Girls Thea Bowman Institute for Excellence and Leadership Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Catalogs & Policies Campus Visit Us About Alverno About A Hispanic-Serving Institution First-Generation College Students Where All Belong Alverno's President Campus Events Campus Life Residence Life Dining Services Student Activities Greenhouse Campus Ministry Campus Safety Store A-Store (Alverno Gear) Resources Academic Academic Advising Career Studio Instructional Services Library Student Development and Success Study Abroad Technology Media Hub Tech Services Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Accounts Student Accounts Financial Aid Health & Safety Wellness Campus Safety Additional Resources Resources for Parents All Student Resources Internal Event Brand Guide Alverno Publications 8 Abilities 8 Abilities Center for Learning and Assessment Support Volunteer Assessor Program Assessment Workshops & Consulting Alverno News Faculty Experts News/Blog A Magazine Apply Request Info Athletics Visit Events Alumnae Give My Alverno Career Education Employer Resources Employer Resources Career Student Resources Career Coaching Internship Advising Internship Advising Forms Recent Internships Handshake Alum Resources Handshake Employer Resources Hire an Intern Recruit a Grad Handshake Internship Forms Community Resources Online Resources Career Studio Team Office Hours & Contact Info About Employer Resources Alverno is one of the nation’s largest Catholic women’s colleges. It offers weekday undergraduate programs for women, as well as evening undergraduate and graduate programs for\n        women and men. Alverno College is consistently ranked among the top Midwest Universities in the U.S. News & World Report for \"Strong Commitment to Teaching\" and \"Most Innovative.”\n        It is also known for: an ability-based curriculum that prepares our students with the competencies necessary for success in the work place a wide variety of majors in Business, Healthcare, STEM, Education, Social Sciences, and Humanities a diverse student population, and is Wisconsin's first Hispanic Serving Institution an award-winning internship program, with most students in our weekday college program required to complete at least one internship in her major Ready for what's next Request More Info Apply Now Explore Programs 3400 S. 43rd St. Milwaukee, WI 53219 414-382-6000 admissions@alverno.edu Campus Map Mesa Location Contact Us Employment at Alverno Event Spaces Faculty Directory Trustees Privacy Policy Faculty & Staff Intranet Accreditation Harassment/Discrimination Policy Web Accessibility Statement Institutional Review Board © Alverno College, All Rights Reserved"
    },
    "https://www.alverno.edu/Career-Hire-an-Intern": {
      "title": "Hire an Alverno Intern",
      "description": "Hire an Intern | Career Studio | Alverno College https://alverno.studentadvisor.ai/virtualadvisor Alverno News Faculty Experts News/Blog Alverno Magazine Athletics Visit Events Alumnae Give My Alverno Search by Keywords\n                  Here Academics & Admissions Academics Majors and Programs List Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Adult Learning & Degree Completion Transfer Students International Students Tuition & Aid Tuition Financial Aid Scholarships Admissions Visit Meet an Admissions Counselor Accepted Students Support & Career Center for Academic Excellence Internships Only at Alverno Research Center for Women and Girls Thea Bowman Institute for Excellence and Leadership Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Catalogs & Policies Campus Visit Us The best way to know if Alverno is right for you is to come visit! About Alverno About A Hispanic-Serving Institution First-Generation College Students Where All Belong Alverno's President Campus Events Campus Life Residence Life Dining Services Student Engagement Greenhouse Campus Ministry Campus Safety Store A-Store (Alverno Gear) Resources Academic Academic Advising Career Studio Center for Learning and Assessment Support Library/Archives Student Development and Success Study Abroad Technology Media Hub Tech Services Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Accounts Student Accounts Financial Aid Health & Safety Wellness Campus Safety Additional Resources Resources for Parents All Student Resources Internal Event Brand Guide Alverno Publications Abilities 8 Abilities Center for Learning and Assessment Support Volunteer Assessor Program Assessment Workshops and Consulting Request Info Apply Menu Close Search by Keywords\n                  Here Academics & Admission Academics Majors and Programs List Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Adult Learning & Degree Completion Transfer Students International Students Tuition & Aid Tuition Financial Aid Scholarships Admissions Visit Meet an Admissions Counselor Accepted Students Support & Career Center for Academic Excellence Internships Only at Alverno Research Center for Women and Girls Thea Bowman Institute for Excellence and Leadership Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Catalogs & Policies Campus Visit Us About Alverno About A Hispanic-Serving Institution First-Generation College Students Where All Belong Alverno's President Campus Events Campus Life Residence Life Dining Services Student Activities Greenhouse Campus Ministry Campus Safety Store A-Store (Alverno Gear) Resources Academic Academic Advising Career Studio Instructional Services Library Student Development and Success Study Abroad Technology Media Hub Tech Services Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Accounts Student Accounts Financial Aid Health & Safety Wellness Campus Safety Additional Resources Resources for Parents All Student Resources Internal Event Brand Guide Alverno Publications 8 Abilities 8 Abilities Center for Learning and Assessment Support Volunteer Assessor Program Assessment Workshops & Consulting Alverno News Faculty Experts News/Blog A Magazine Apply Request Info Athletics Visit Events Alumnae Give My Alverno Career Education Hire an Alverno Intern Hire an Alverno Intern Career Student Resources Career Coaching Internship Advising Internship Advising Forms Recent Internships Handshake Alum Resources Handshake Employer Resources Hire an Intern Recruit a Grad Handshake Internship Forms Community Resources Online Resources Career Studio Team Office Hours & Contact Info Advantages to Employers How will you benefit by mentoring an Alverno intern? You will have an opportunity to: Get needed work done that might not otherwise be completed See your work/procedures etc. from the perspective of a fresh pair of eyes Recruit/screen possible new hires Have the satisfaction of assisting a student in her educational growth and development Contribute to the development of qualified workers for the future Connect with faculty and bridge the gap between education and the world of work AND as an additional bonus: Your intern is prepared for work by the rigorous training of Alverno's curriculum. Your intern is supported by Alverno faculty to help her succeed in her internship. She either attends a seminar or is monitored individually by faculty from her discipline department for\n        the duration of the internship. Your intern is highly motivated. She needs to successfully complete her work with you in order to receive academic credit for the internship. Internship Process Process for offering internships to Alverno students: Identify a project or ongoing work of a professional nature. Create a job description that includes the skills a student would need to have. Post the opportunity on Handshake , our electronic job board. Internship opportunities should be made available well in advance of the semester you\n        need an intern (January for summer and fall internships, and September for spring internships). Interested students will send their resume. Interview and select an intern. Review the requirements for employers below. Requirements for Employers What will you have to do as a mentor? Interview and select an intern. Make arrangements with the intern for dates and times she will work. We require students to work at the site 8 to 12 hours a week for the duration of the semester, or 120 to 180 hours\n        total during the summer. Orient the intern to the site. Clearly explain the project or work you wish the intern to do. Provide the resources the intern will need. Provide direction and give feedback on an ongoing basis. Meet with us at your site (or by Zoom) for a mid-semester check-in regarding how the student is doing. Fill out and/or sign four internship forms which track and document the intern's progress: A description of the student's work at the site (to be filled out by the mentor) A description (to be filled out by the student) of their learning goals for this site A mid-term evaluation of the student (to be filled out by the mentor and reviewed with the student) A final evaluation of the student (to be filled out by the mentor and reviewed with the student) Ready for what's next Request More Info Apply Now Explore Programs 3400 S. 43rd St. Milwaukee, WI 53219 414-382-6000 admissions@alverno.edu Campus Map Mesa Location Contact Us Employment at Alverno Event Spaces Faculty Directory Trustees Privacy Policy Faculty & Staff Intranet Accreditation Harassment/Discrimination Policy Web Accessibility Statement Institutional Review Board © Alverno College, All Rights Reserved"
    },
